-- Counter state machine: maintains Count ≥ 0.
--
-- A state machine is State × Event ⇝ State. As an arrow graph:
--   state_machine = rec { (arr("state.inc") ||| arr("state.dec")) >>> first(id) }
--
-- where handle_event updates the state based on the event, and first(id)
-- passes the event stream through unchanged (side channel).
--
-- The counter processes events that either increment or decrement the count.
-- The state.dec atom has requires: Le(0, input) and guarantee: Le(0, output),
-- so the fixpoint discovers Le(0, count) (Count ≥ 0) as the invariant.
--
-- Invariant: Le(0, count) -- INFERRED (Count ≥ 0, discovered by fixpoint).
-- Termination: Constant (side-channel; event stream passes through).

rec { (arr("state.inc") ||| arr("state.dec")) >>> first(id) }
